More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (781–790)
781. Improper Validation of API Version Headers
API Version Header Manipulation
Attackers manipulate API version headers to access deprecated or insecure API versions.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
782. Insecure Handling of File Thumbnail Generation
Thumbnail Processing Exploit
Thumbnail generators process malicious files that may lead to code execution or data leakage.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
783. Improper Validation of User Blocking Features
User Block Bypass
Blocked users can still interact with the victim due to weak enforcement.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
784. Insecure Handling of Contact Import Features
Contact Import Data Exposure
Contact import tools leak private email addresses or phone numbers.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
785. Improper Validation of Audit Log Access
Audit Log Authorization Bypass
Attackers access audit logs belonging to other organizations or users.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
786. Insecure Handling of Notification Delivery APIs
Notification Delivery Manipulation
Attackers send fake system notifications to users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
787. Improper Validation of Data Import Tools
Data Import Injection
CSV or data import tools allow injection of malicious formulas or commands.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
788. Insecure Handling of Password Strength Validation
Weak Password Policy Enforcement
Systems accept extremely weak passwords despite security policies.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
789. Improper Validation of Account Activity APIs
Account Activity Disclosure
Attackers access activity history belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
790. Insecure Handling of Service Configuration APIs
Service Configuration Exposure
Configuration APIs expose sensitive service settings.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
